MVP Responsibilities

For Ohira v0.1, the Core Engine must support:

Configuration loading

Project scanning

Plugin discovery

Sequential and parallel plugin execution

Knowledge Graph construction

Report generation

AI Context generation

Incremental analysis

Error isolation

Basic metrics



---

Engineering Guidelines

The Core Engine should:

Remain under active test coverage.

Expose stable public interfaces.

Avoid framework-specific assumptions.

Minimize startup time.

Support future distributed execution without major redesign.



---

Guiding Principle

> "The Core Engine coordinates intelligence; plugins provide expertise."



This separation ensures Ohira can continue to support new technologies, frameworks, and workflows without requiring changes to its central architecture.
